"answer": "\\min(X, Y) \\sim \\text{Exp}(2\\lambda)",
"explanation": "The proposed solution is correct. It correctly applies the survival function method for independent random variables. Specifically, it correctly identifies that \\{\\min(X, Y) > z\\} is equivalent to \\{X > z\\} \\cap \\{Y > z\\}, uses the independence property to multiply the individual survival functions \\(e^{-\\lambda z}\\), and correctly identifies the resulting function \\(e^{-2\\lambda z}\\) as the survival function of an exponential distribution with parameter \\(2\\lambda\\)."
